 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 6.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 5.7, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.5 to 9.4. December accounts for 13% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 8% of all its works contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 6. Contract [1], for 39,750 euros, was awarded in November 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the limit threshold does not indicate improper conduct. It could reflect market pricing, budget constraints, or separate needs. Statistical patterns alone do not prove wrongdoing or mismanagement.\nWhat can be checked: Check the contract details for [1] to see what was purchased and the dates. Verify if awardee A has other contracts for similar services. Review if multiple contracts were used for the same purpose to ensure consistency in procurement.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"obras","citas":["j8jybJzY4oCkU02jNGj1Fw%3D%3D","r9zr5eJTn0rmnwcj%2BxbdTg%3D%3D","IRTCMiCcrF6cTfjQf3USOg%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}